  2 diagonals are chosen. The number of ways to choose 2 diagonals from a 7-gon is \(\binom{14}{2}\) (since a 7-gon has 14 diagonals). The number of ways to choose 4 vertices from 7 (which determine a pair of intersecting diagonals) is \(\binom{7}{4}\). The probability is the ratio of these two quantities.  \[
\frac{\binom{7}{4}}{\binom{14}{2}} = \frac{\frac{7 \cdot 6 \cdot 5 \cdot 4}{4 \cdot 3 \cdot 2 \cdot 1}}{\frac{14 \cdot 13}{2 \cdot 1}} = \frac{35}{91} = \frac{5}{13}
</think> <answer> \boxed{\frac{5}{13}} </answer>

